% Bibliography for report/main.tex.
%
% Every entry here is one of the works of build specification section 25, which is the
% reference list the August 2026 literature survey assembled and verified. Ground rule 1
% forbids inventing a citation, so nothing is added to that list and nothing in it is
% embellished: the journal, volume, issue and year of each entry are the ones the
% specification records, and an identifier appears only where the specification gives it
% (the arXiv ids) or where it is a fact about the work rather than a lookup. No DOI is
% written here, because a DOI recalled rather than resolved is exactly the kind of
% unverifiable detail ground rule 1 bans, and an arXiv id or a journal, volume and year
% locate the work anyway.
%
% No page ranges anywhere, deliberately. BibTeX joins a first and last page with the two
% hyphen sequence that TeX turns into an en dash, and ground rule 3 bans that sequence from
% the report, so this file never gives BibTeX a pair of pages to join. Works are located
% by volume, issue and year, and by article number where the journal uses one, which is
% enough to find any of them. See docs/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md, 2026-08-31.
%
% Two entries, westermann2026 and gopakumar2026, carry a note saying that their author list
% and title are abbreviated as the survey recorded them rather than transcribed from the
% published article. That note prints in the bibliography. Writing a full author list I
% cannot verify would be the fabrication the note exists to avoid.


